[lease] card | #   load) as gemm32 past 8 rows; routed and shared experts through iq2_xxs_gemv_sel. Engine's band [derived]:
[lease] card | #   500..1000 tok/s at P = 512, the experts' per-slot _sel rereads (~370 GB a 448-row pass) the dominant term.
[lease] card | # - G1 bolt-prefill-g1 f7063282: E1 rebased on the IQ2_XXS grouped GEMM (routed and shared experts as GEMMs).
[lease] card | #   Engine's band [derived]: 800..1600 tok/s at P = 512 (the per-slot rereads leave), target >= 820.
[lease] card | # Both load-checked by engine on the real file (resident 27.41 GB with the Q8_0 twins, 24 greedy ids = --prefill step).
[lease] card | kind: baseline
[lease] card | question: how fast do E1's and G1's batched prefills read a 512- and a 4096-id Bolt prompt on the A6000, against
[lease] card |   main's steps?
[lease] card | term: pp tok/s @ P = 512 (the row's pp_tok/s), bin arm generate_qwen3moe built at 39fff4df, RTX A6000; the
[lease] card |   f7063282 arm is read beside it against 800..1600
[lease] card | unit: tok/s
[lease] card | predict: 500..1000
[lease] card | condition: one lease, BLOOMERY_CARD=a6000, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2; arms 512 4096 (main) and the two bin arms at 512 and
[lease] card |   4096; busy tags read beside each mean
[lease] card | reason: the Bolt speed plan's prefill stage 1; why now: E1 and G1 load on the real file and the lead's deadline is
[lease] card |   20:40
[lease] card | decide-in: E1/G1 are the plan's prefill stage 1; G2/G3 and the chunked scan are priced from the gap to llama.cpp's
[lease] card |   1549 (-ub 512) / 1890 (-ub 1024)
[lease] card | decide-below: a per-pass term is larger than derived: nsys the pass before the next stage
[lease] card | decide-above: the experts' L2 reuse covers more than derived: re-derive the next stage's gain
[lease] card: ok kind=baseline (no ruler: not an ab card)
